# The pins of scope_surface.rs (HT-SURF, §5.2 Q-LEXSCOPE LS1 part 4, DELTA10 L1 / L2), one
# section per table: a line `== NAME` opens it ; `#` lines are notes ; a table is tab-separated,
# its first line a header ; a COUNTS / PRESENT section is one line compared verbatim.
# SURF_* = the real crate's (`crate::lexscope`) ; FIX_* = the fixture modules'
# (scope_surface.fixtures). SURF_VOCAB / SURF_TRAITS are the vocabulary both use. LS1 part 5
# (DELTA11 R2) adds the counted lists CARD, CB, BODY and the hash column of MACROS, each with
# its FIX_ twin ; LS1 part 6 adds INTERIOR's exemptions (SURF_INTERIOR, empty, and FIX_INTERIOR) ;
# with the module absent every SURF_ list is empty (a row is STALE). LS1 part 7 (DELTA12 S1 S2
# N-1 N-6) adds ADDR (ADDR_NAMES, SURF_ADDR, SURF_ADDR_CALLS), UNWIND (SURF_UNWIND, empty) and
# ENTER's `holds` column (IN-TOTAL), each list with its FIX_ twin.
# LS2a (§5.2 Q-LEXSCOPE) flips SURF_PRESENT to `present` and pins the first rows: LEAVE L1-L3, ENTER 6, CB 2,
# INTERIOR 1, MACROS `zn`, E / BODY / ROWS / OUT_TYPES as computed, SURF_PLAN's 4 LS2a fns at lexscope/elab.rs.
== ADDR_TOOLCHAIN
# the toolchain ADDR_NAMES was read against (rust-toolchain.toml's channel ; a bump re-reads it)
1.85.0
== ADDR_NAMES
# ADDR's NAMED forms (DELTA12 S1): n1 the path segment (`ptr ::` / `:: ptr` / any `use` of it) ;
# n2 an ident anywhere ; n3 a method `. name (` or a path `:: name`. A closed list of std's API
# for 1.85.0: a std fn off it that takes a reference and reveals its address is not seen (L-8)
form	name
n1	ptr
n2	addr_of
n2	addr_of_mut
n2	NonNull
n2	Pointer
n2	transmute
n3	ptr_eq
n3	as_ptr
n3	as_mut_ptr
n3	as_ptr_range
n3	as_mut_ptr_range
n3	into_raw
n3	addr
n3	expose_provenance
n3	expose_addr
n3	element_offset
n3	subslice_range
n3	substr_range
== SURF_ADDR
# ADDR (DELTA12 S1): every address site of crates/elaborate/src, crate-wide (module or not):
# file · fn (nested fns joined by `::`, `-` outside a fn) · form · count · OPERAND (the token
# text of each converted expression, ` | `-joined in source order). A site off it FAILS ADDR ;
# a row matching nothing is STALE
file	fn	form	count	operand
gen_enum.rs	gen_carried_typedefs	n1:ptr	1	(* f , it)
hoist/general.rs	enclosing_call_cannot_read	n1:ptr	1	(d , * a)
hoist/general_query.rs	arg_is_input_at	n1:ptr	1	(* a as * const ast :: Expr , target)
hoist/general_query.rs	arg_is_input_at	s1:*const	2	& args [i] | * a
wext.rs	conn_expr_addr	s1:*const	1	e
== SURF_ADDR_CALLS
# CALLS: the identifier tokens of each address fn's name crate-wide, the `fn <name>` excluded
# DK1-0 (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY, DELTA14 D3 A1): ports.rs:740's address left wire_ports for the leaf wext.rs conn_expr_addr (one caller)
fn	calls
arg_is_input_at	2
conn_expr_addr	1
enclosing_call_cannot_read	1
gen_carried_typedefs	1
== SURF_UNWIND
# UNWIND (DELTA12 N-6): catch_unwind / set_hook / take_hook / resume_unwind / panic_any tokens
# in crates/elaborate/src ; pinned empty
file	fn	name	count
== SURF_VOCAB
# HT's table of opaque lexscope types: plan10/g/surface.tsv's 12 TYPE rows (DELTA10 L1 I-SURF's
# list: ScopeRef, Saved, the witness = ScopeWitness (DELTA9's name, not yet checked by names.py),
# Shown, ShownCtx, ScopeKeyed<V>, SavedChain, SavedRoot, SavedMethod, ReportedAt ; Scopes (the
# tier-K receiver) ; Mark, the mark selector, an enum: also on ENUMS when it exists) + DK1's
# NewKey, AtKey, DeclKey, Keyed<V> ; DK1-1 (§5.2 Q-DECLKEY) adds Keyed's set twin KeyedSet (lexscope/key.rs).
# A name here passes only where the file set DEFINES it as
# the kind written.
name	kind
Scopes	struct
Saved	struct
ScopeWitness	struct
Shown	struct
ShownCtx	struct
SavedChain	struct
SavedRoot	struct
SavedMethod	struct
ScopeRef	struct
ScopeKeyed	struct
Mark	enum
ReportedAt	struct
NewKey	struct
AtKey	struct
DeclKey	struct
Keyed	struct
KeyedSet	struct
== SURF_TRAITS
# the crate-visible traits allowed (plan10/g/surface.tsv: 1, the boundary trait)
name
Outgoing
== SURF_MACROS
# MACRO-BODY (DELTA11 R2): every `macro_rules!` the file set defines, or the rest of the crate
# defines and the file set calls, with the sha256 of its token tree ; also the item-position
# macros allowed. Empty until the module exists (a row with no definition is STALE): `zn`'s row
# and hash come with LS2a (DELTA11 R6), read by its delta judge (NP-5).
name	sha256
zn	d8f9c54aafb2a97e923fc75a6a47a199be52921f7246d60927f08b10862815cf
== SURF_PRESENT
present
== SURF_COUNTS
present=present files=5 rows=156 out_types=24 e_fns=29 text_flows=42
